parts.text:
Both confirmed. Final plan:

## Plan — fix Hero→features skip when returning

Keep the current scroll-triggered navigation to `features` (no auto-scroll), and replay the sequence on return.

**`components/sections/UserNeeds.tsx`**
- Add a `useEffect` with a passive `window` scroll listener that, when `userneeds` is clearly **below** the viewport (user scrolled back up to `hero`), resets both `introDone` and `sequenceDone` to `false`:
  ```ts
  useEffect(() => {
    const section = sectionRef.current;
    if (!section) return;
    const onScroll = () => {
      if (section.getBoundingClientRect().top > window.innerHeight * 0.4) {
        setIntroDone(false);
        setSequenceDone(false);
      }
    };
    window.addEventListener("scroll", onScroll, { passive: true });
    return () => window.removeEventListener("scroll", onScroll);
  }, []);
  ```
- Keep `useScrollNextSection(sectionRef, "#features", sequenceDone)`.

**Why it fixes the bug:** while at `hero`, `sequenceDone` is now `false`, so `UserNeeds`' hijack to `#features` is disabled — only `Hero`'s hijack (`#userneeds`) fires, so the user goes back into `userneeds`. The sequence replays (intro→words→outro), then finish enables the `features` hijack again. Scrolling from `userneeds` down to `features` leaves it above the viewport (negative top), so it won't spuriously reset.

**Verify:** `npm run lint` and `npm run build`.

Toggle out of plan mode to implement.

