parts.text:
Confirmed. Here's the final plan.

## Plan: Per-card staggered reveal for HowItWorks cards

**`components/ui/how-it-works.tsx`** only (no section-file changes needed):

1. Add `useReducedMotion` to the existing `motion/react` import:
   ```ts
   import { LazyMotion, domAnimation, m, useReducedMotion } from "motion/react";
   ```
2. In the `HowItWorks` component, add `const reduced = useReducedMotion();`.
3. In `data.map`, wrap each `<Card>` in an `<m.div>` that drives the reveal, and move the positional/tilt classes onto that wrapper:
   ```tsx
   <m.div
     key={step.title}
     initial={reduced ? { opacity: 0 } : { opacity: 0, y: 28, scale: 0.96 }}
     whileInView={reduced ? { opacity: 1 } : { opacity: 1, y: 0, scale: 1 }}
     viewport={{ once: true, margin: "-80px" }}
     transition={{ duration: 0.6, ease: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1], delay: index * 0.15 }}
     className={`${position.className} ${position.rotate}`.trim()}
   >
     <Card
       number={`0${index + 1}`}
       title={step.title}
       description={step.description}
       colorTheme={step.colorTheme || "blue"}
       colors={step.colors}
     />
   </m.div>
   ```
4. Update `<Card>` usage to drop the old `rotate={position.rotate}` / `className={position.className}` (positioning now lives on the wrapper; Card keeps its own sizing/hover classes).

**Behavior:**
- On scroll into view, each card fades up + scales in sequentially (0.15s stagger), matching the site's `easeOutExpo`.
- Desktop absolute placement + tilt preserved (classes moved to wrapper; Tailwind v4 `rotate` is its own CSS property, so it composes fine with framer's transform).
- Mobile stacked layout unaffected (position classes are `md:`-scoped).
- Reduced-motion users get a plain opacity fade.
- LazyMotion is already wrapping the tree, so no extra setup.

**Verify:** `npm run lint` and `npm run build`.

Toggle out of plan mode when ready and I'll implement.

