Let's fix line 207 (unescaped quote):
Change `"{quoteText}"` to `&ldquo;{quoteText}&rdquo;` or `&quot;{quoteText}&quot;`.

And fix the `setState` in `useEffect` at lines 233-239:
Instead of setting state in an effect depending on `customTestimonials`, we can use `prevProp` comparison or compute initial state or update state when `customTestimonials` changes using key or state initializer function or comparing `customTestimonials !== prevProps`.
Actually, if `key={customTestimonials?.length}` is used on `StaggerTestimonials` or if we calculate `initialData` dynamically when `customTestimonials` changes during render:

```tsx
  const [prevTestimonials, setPrevTestimonials] = useState(customTestimonials);
  const [testimonialsList, setTestimonialsList] = useState(() => 
    (customTestimonials && customTestimonials.length > 0 ? customTestimonials : DEFAULT_TESTIMONIALS).map((item, idx) => ({
      ...item,
      tempId: item.tempId ?? idx
    }))
  );

  if (customTestimonials !== prevTestimonials) {
    setPrevTestimonials(customTestimonials);
    setTestimonialsList(
      (customTestimonials && customTestimonials.length > 0 ? customTestimonials : DEFAULT_TESTIMONIALS).map((item, idx) => ({
        ...item,
        tempId: item.tempId ?? idx
      }))
    );
  }
```
In React 19 / latest React, updating state *during render* when props change is the officially recommended pattern for syncing state from props (instead of inside `useEffect`).

Let's edit `components/ui/stagger-testimonials.tsx`.

