The user asks: "modifikasi agar bisa di swipe kiri kanan" (modify so it can be swiped left and right).

Let's look at `components/ui/stagger-testimonials.tsx`.
Currently, card movement is handled by `handleMove(1)` (move right / next) and `handleMove(-1)` (move left / prev), or clicking on cards.
To support touch/mouse swipe gestures (drag/swipe left & right):
We can add touch/pointer handlers on the container (`onTouchStart`, `onTouchMove`, `onTouchEnd`, `onMouseDown`, `onMouseMove`, `onMouseUp`, `onMouseLeave` or `PointerEvents`).

Let's design a clean, responsive drag/swipe handler:
- We track `touchStartX` or `pointerStartX`.
- When user swipes left (delta X < -50), we call `handleMove(1)` (advance to next).
- When user swipes right (delta X > 50), we call `handleMove(-1)` (go to prev).
- We should ensure text selection / image dragging doesn't interfere (e.g. `select-none`, `touch-pan-y` or `touch-none`).
- We can add touch handlers:
  - `onTouchStart` / `onTouchMove` / `onTouchEnd`
  - `onPointerDown` / `onPointerMove` / `onPointerUp` / `onPointerCancel`

Let's check details of swipe gesture logic:
```tsx
  const [touchStart, setTouchStart] = useState<number | null>(null);
  const [touchEnd, setTouchEnd] = useState<number | null>(null);

  // Minimum swipe distance threshold (in px)
  const minSwipeDistance = 40;

  const onTouchStart = (e: React.TouchEvent | React.MouseEvent) => {
    const clientX = 'touches' in e ? e.touches[0].clientX : e.clientX;
    setTouchEnd(null);
    setTouchStart(clientX);
  };

  const onTouchMove = (e: React.TouchEvent | React.MouseEvent) => {
    if (touchStart === null) return;
    const clientX = 'touches' in e ? e.touches[0].clientX : e.clientX;
    setTouchEnd(clientX);
  };

  const onTouchEnd = () => {
    if (!touchStart || !touchEnd) return;
    const distance = touchStart - touchEnd;
    const isLeftSwipe = distance > minSwipeDistance;
    const isRightSwipe = distance < -minSwipeDistance;

    if (isLeftSwipe) {
      handleMove(1); // Swipe left = next
    } else if (isRightSwipe) {
      handleMove(-1); // Swipe right = prev
    }

    setTouchStart(null);
    setTouchEnd(null);
  };
```

