If `onClick` is on `TestimonialCard`:
When user clicks (without dragging or diffX < 5px), `handleMove(position)` on `TestimonialCard` fires.
If user drags > 40px, `handleDragEnd` fires `handleMove(1)` or `handleMove(-1)`.
To avoid `onClick` triggering when dragging, `handleCardClick` can check if `Math.abs((dragStartX.current || 0) - (dragEndX.current || 0)) > 10`.

